<% content_for :title, "Pythagorean Theorem Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Pythagorean Theorem calculator page (spec issue #253, DESIGN.md BLEND). A leaner sibling
  of Right Triangle: the picker selects WHICH SIDE is unknown (the `mode`) — both legs (a, b)
  are given (solve the hypotenuse c), or one leg and the hypotenuse (a, c) are given (solve
  the other leg b) — and the page solves the missing side via a² + b² = c². The form posts
  over Turbo and re-renders the #result region in place; it works WITHOUT JS — the server
  validates exactly the selected mode's two given sides and re-renders the result fragment.
  Stimulus is pure polish: it reveals the side fields the chosen mode needs and lifts the
  active option row.

  Mode-picker choice (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"): TWO modes, each a MULTI-WORD label
  ("Solve the hypotenuse" / "Solve a leg"). N ≤ 3 but multi-word → the selectable option
  list (.mode-option), NOT a segmented control (reserved for N ≤ 3 SHORT labels) and not a
  raw <select> (only N > ~8). It stays a native radio <fieldset>/<legend> posting a
  single-select inputs[mode].

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to
  one column on mobile. Spacing ("targets not minimums"): stacked fields → space-y-5; major
  blocks within the card → mt-8 (Section tier); column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8.
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Math · Geometry</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Pythagorean Theorem Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    In a right triangle, <span class="font-semibold text-ink">a² + b² = c²</span> — the squares of
    the two legs <span class="font-semibold text-ink">a</span> and <span class="font-semibold text-ink">b</span>
    sum to the square of the hypotenuse <span class="font-semibold text-ink">c</span>. Enter any two
    sides and the missing one is solved server-side, with a labeled figure of the triangle.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/pythagorean_theorem", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "pythagorean-theorem" } do |f| %>

      <%# Mode picker — selectable option list (.mode-option), per DESIGN.md §4: two
          multi-word solve-for modes → one bordered, divided container of full-width rows.
          The accessible control is a native radio <fieldset>/<legend> posting inputs[mode];
          each radio is visually-hidden (peer sr-only) and paired to a styled <label for>.
          The active row paints with no JS via peer:checked, and the .mode-option::before
          radio glyph is the non-colour active cue (DESIGN.md §6). Each row names the two
          GIVEN sides (label) and, on a helper line, the side that mode solves. %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Solve for…</legend>
        <div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-[13px] border border-border-input divide-y divide-rule">
          <% pythagorean_theorem_modes.each_with_index do |m, i| %>
            <div>
              <%= f.radio_button :mode, m[:value],
                    checked: i.zero?,
                    class: "peer sr-only",
                    data: { pythagorean_theorem_target: "modeInput", action: "pythagorean-theorem#select" } %>
              <%= f.label :mode, value: m[:value],
                    class: "mode-option",
                    data: { pythagorean_theorem_target: "pill", mode: m[:value] } do %>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink"><%= m[:label] %></span>
                <span class="text-xs text-muted"><%= m[:solves] %></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Side fields. Each block declares the modes it serves via
          data-pythagorean-theorem-modes; Stimulus shows only the active mode's blocks and
          disables the rest so they aren't submitted (the no-JS baseline shows all three —
          the server reads only the mode's two given sides). Leg a is shared by both modes.
          Stacked tier: space-y-5 down the column (DESIGN.md §3); each input carries its
          side-symbol affix on the Affix tier (gap-2). %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# Leg a — given in BOTH modes. %>
        <div data-pythagorean-theorem-target="field" data-pythagorean-theorem-modes="hypotenuse leg">
          <%= f.label :a, "Leg a", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_a" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :a, id: "inputs_a", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal", min: "0",
                  placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-7 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">a</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Leg b — given only in `hypotenuse` mode. %>
        <div data-pythagorean-theorem-target="field" data-pythagorean-theorem-modes="hypotenuse">
          <%= f.label :b, "Leg b", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_b" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :b, id: "inputs_b", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal", min: "0",
                  placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-7 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">b</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Hypotenuse c — given only in `leg` mode; must exceed leg a. %>
        <div data-pythagorean-theorem-target="field" data-pythagorean-theorem-modes="leg">
          <%= f.label :c, "Hypotenuse (c)", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_c" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :c, id: "inputs_c", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal", min: "0",
                  placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-7 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">c</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
